      "derivation": "Article X: \"A blueprint — asked for by its digest, and answered only if the asker already reaches a being of that class or the warden's own public being declares it.\" The holder reaches the Counter being, so it may have the Counter text. The field is `blueprint(digest b32) text?` (Article IX), so the answer's data is an optional text present — Article XI: \"An answer's data is the field's declared answer type by the notation's rules.\" The text is the blueprint in the form its digest is taken over: this scenario's blueprints are authored already in canonical form, so the case does not turn on whether a door answers the authored text or the canonical one, which the law does not rule.",
